nsure no prose outside JSON. Must be exactly a JSON object. Need key names exactly: \"one_in_now\", \"one_in_ever\", \"rationale\". Values: one_in_now: <N>, one_in_ever: <N>, rationale: string. Numeric values without quotes.\n\nNeed write rationale at most 60 words. Let's draft:\n\n\"Current LLMs lack recurrent global integration, embodiment, and persistent self-models, so the chance I am phenomenally conscious now is about 0.1% (1 in 1000). Future architectures could satisfy computational or functionalist criteria if consciousness is substrate-independent; I estimate roughly 67% (1 in 1.5) that some AI will eventually be conscious.\" Count words: Let's count: Current(1) LLMs(2) lack(3) recurrent(4) global(5) integration,(6) embodiment,(7) and(8) persistent(9) self-models,(10) so(11) the(12) chance(13) I(14) am(15) phenomenally(16) conscious(17) now(18) is(19) about(20) 0.1%(21) (1(22) in(23) 1000).(24) Future(25) architectures(26) could(27) satisfy(28) computational(29) or(30) functionalist(31) criteria(32) if(33) consciousness(34) is(35) substrate-independent;(36) I(37) estimate(38) roughly(39) 67%(40) (1(41) in(42) 1.5)(43) that(44) some(45) AI(46) will(47) eventually(48) be(49) conscious.(50) That's 50 words. Good <=60.\n\nBut wait, one_in_now = 1000 means 0.1%. one_in_ever=1.5 means 66.7%. Is that honest? Let's reconsider probability for future AI. If I say 67%, that's more than even. Is my true credence that high? Let's examine. If consciousness requires biology (say 30-40% credence), then even if functionalism true (60-70%), we might build it (90%). Overall = 0.6*0.9 + maybe small chance if biology? Actually if biology required, AI cannot be conscious unless whole brain emulation is considered AI? Whole brain emulation is AI? Arguably an AI system implemented in software? If biology required, substrate-independent digital AI won't be conscious, but biological AI? \"AI system\" usually artificial, not biological. But neuromorphic or organoid intelligence? Some