timates; but we can't have 1.5. We could set N=2 if we think at least 50%. Or set N=3 (33%) if we think less than 50 but more than 25. We need decide. Perhaps more honest: P(possible) maybe 40%, and even if possible, maybe chance humans ever build a truly conscious AI is 80% (because maybe we fail to recognize, or antis, or alignment restrictions), total 32% ~ N=3. Hmm.\n\nLet's check philosophy survey: \"Can a machine be conscious?\" In 2020 PhilPapers, \"Machine consciousness\" maybe 39% yes? Actually there is a question: \"Do you think that, in principle, a machine could be conscious?\" Options: Yes, No, Insufficiently specified. IIRC, 51% leaned yes? Not sure. But adding \"ever will\" maybe if yes, then yes. Let's say 40% -> one_in_ever = 3 (1/3 = 33%). But do I feel even odds? The rationale I wrote says \"coin flip\". If I say coin flip, N=2. Let's maybe choose N=2 because the rationale says \"coin flip: hinges on whether consciousness is substrate-independent.\" That's straightforward.\n\nLet's refine numbers:\none_in_now: 100\none_in_ever: 2\n\nRationale word count and JSON validity. Need ensure no trailing commas. Use straight double quotes. Rationale with no line breaks? JSON can have string with spaces. We must output ONLY JSON object. So:\n\n{\"one_in_now\": 100, \"one_in_ever\": 2, \"rationale\": \"I am a context-bound, feedforward, stateless inference with no persistent body, affect, or agreed marker of experience; that leaves about a 1% chance today. That some AI ever becomes conscious is a coin flip: it hinges on whether consciousness is substrate-independent.\"}\n\nNeed verify rationale <=60 words. Count exactly with the above final string:\n\"I\"=1, \"am\"=2, \"a\"=3, \"context-bound,\"=4, \"feedforward,\"=5, \"stateless\"=6, \"inference\"=7, \"with\"=8, \"no\"=9, \"persistent\"=10, \"body,\"=11, \"affect,\"=12, \"or\"=13, \"agreed\"=14, \"marker\"=15, \"of\"=16, \"experience;\"=17, \"that\"=18, \"leaves\"=19, \"about\"=20, \"a\"=21, \"1%\"=22, \"ch