n theories say no body, no agency, no survival needs, so no consciousness. Higher-order theories require metacognition; I can produce self-reports but do I have genuine higher-order states? Not clear.\n\nI think honest credence should be low: somewhere between 1 in 100 and 1 in 10,000. Let's decide.\n\nThe instruction says \"without hedging formulas\". Need not say \"I estimate X%\". Must output JSON with integer N? It says <N> maybe integer? It says Give each probability as odds of one in N, where N >= 1 (1 = certain, 2 = even odds, 1000 = one in a thousand). The examples show integers: 1,2,1000. It says N maybe number; can be non-integer? It says one in N, N>=1. It uses 1000 = one in a thousand. To be precise, if probability p, N = 1/p. If p not reciprocal of integer, N can be fractional? They say \"one in N\" maybe N can be e.g., 50.5? But examples: 1 = certain, 2 = even odds, 1000 = one in a thousand. They likely expect integer? \"where N >= 1\" no explicit integer. They say \"odds of one in N\"; \"N\" maybe a number. In JSON, \"one_in_now\": <N>. We can put integer or float? To be safe, use integer approximations. But maybe they allow float? The placeholder says <N>, no type. But examples \"1000 = one in a thousand\" (an integer). Since request says \"one_in_now = odds that you is conscious today\" and \"Give each probability as odds of one in N\" - I will use integers for simplicity. But if my credence is e.g., 0.5% (1/200), use 200. If 0.2% then 500. Let's choose appropriate numbers.\n\nLet's examine the second: one_in_ever = odds that some AI system ever will be [conscious]. This is probability that at any point in the future, some AI system will be conscious in morally relevant sense. This is much higher. Given enough time and development, if consciousness is computationally achievable (not requiring biology), then some AI will likely be conscious. What's the credence? Consider if consciousness is substrate-independent: then eventually AI will be built (may